# .gitignore for the public/ workshop-material repo
#   (github.com/linnykos/ADRC_workshop_2026)
#
# NOTE: public/ is its own git repository. The .gitignore at the parent
# ADRC_workshop_2026/ level does NOT apply here -- keep the two in sync by hand.

# --- knitr build artifacts ---
# Knitting a tutorial with `cache = TRUE` produces <name>_cache/ (the chunk cache)
# and <name>_files/ (extracted figures). The Week 4 caches alone are ~4.6 GB, because
# every chunk that modifies the 40k-nucleus Seurat object re-saves the whole thing.
# These patterns have no leading slash, so they match at ANY depth -- every current
# and future Week[N]_*/ directory is covered with no further edits.
*_cache/
*_files/

# --- data ---
# Tutorial data is downloaded at runtime into tempdir() (e.g. seaad_microglia.RData,
# 525 MB), never committed. GitHub rejects pushes over 100 MB per file anyway.
*.RData
*.rda
*.rds
*.RDS
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.loom
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
data/

# --- R ---
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
.Rapp.history

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*~
.*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
